  "title": "Jack O Lantern Origin: Why Were the First Ones Turnips?",
  "description": "Jack o lantern origin: the first jack-o'-lanterns were not pumpkins at all. They were scary faces carved into turnips in old Ireland. So how did a turnip turn into the grinning pumpkin on your porch?\n\nIn 2026, a Rhode Island pumpkin set a Guinness World Record at 3,156 pounds. But long before giant pumpkins, Irish families hollowed out turnips and other root vegetables for Halloween night. An Irish folk legend tells of Stingy Jack, who tricked the Devil, was shut out of heaven and hell, and wanders with a coal glowing inside a carved turnip. Irish immigrants brought the custom to America, where pumpkins were bigger and easier to carve.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for one strange true story every day. Would you carve a turnip this Halloween? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #jackolantern #halloween #stickstory",
